p14s1","text":"Run it from the project:"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Use `npm link` if you want `taskctl` on your shell path. Set `CODEX_TASKBOARD_URL` to point the CLI "},{"id":"p16s2","text":"at another local or LAN service. Cloud deployments are configured through the **loopback companion**"},{"id":"p16s3","text":" (device-local loopback service for auth and path mapping—not a chat persona) with `taskctl cloud lo"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"ice-local loopback service for auth and path mapping—not a chat persona) with `taskctl cloud login`."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Install the Codex Skill"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Copy or symlink `skills/manage-taskboard` into the Codex skills directory, then start a new Codex ta"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"y or symlink `skills/manage-taskboard` into the Codex skills directory, then start a new Codex task:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"The desktop app keeps this same directory synchronized with its bundled Skill. The Skill teaches Cod"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ex to inspect an issue, move it to `in_progress`, use optimistic versions, verify the work, and then"},{"id":"p20s3","text":" move it to `in_review`; it moves the issue to `done` only after the user explicitly confirms accept"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"ance or asks to mark it complete."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Embed in Codex"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### Manual: use a dedicated CDP port"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Keep the existing Codex window open. From the Taskboard repository, start a second Codex instance wi"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"th a dedicated CDP port:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"After the new Codex window appears, run the injector in another terminal:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Keep the injector terminal running while using the embedded panel. The original Codex window remains"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" unchanged, and the new window receives the Taskboard sidebar entry. If port `9231` is occupied, use"},{"id":"p27s3","text":" another port in both commands."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"### Recommended: launch an independent Taskboard window with one command"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"Keep existing Codex windows open and run:"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"This starts the local Taskboard service when needed. It reuses an open Codex with a reachable CDP re"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"nderer, opens Taskboard in the native browser panel of an ordinary Codex without CDP, or launches th"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"e official macOS Codex app with an independent profile and loopback-only port `9231` when no Codex i"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"s open. It injects a native-looking Taskboard entry after Plugins when CDP is available and keeps wa"},{"id":"p31s5","text":"tching both the service and replacement renderers. Keep this command running while using the embedde"},{"id":"p31s6","text":"d panel. The launcher does not modify `ChatGPT.app` or its `app.asar`."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The source launcher writes its authenticated endpoint to `.data/launcher-runtime.json`. A `taskctl` "},{"id":"p32s2","text":"command installed with `npm link` reads this file by default, so a normal shell and a Codex task ope"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"ned from the panel use the same Taskboard service without an extra environment variable."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"### macOS App: open and inject without a terminal"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"For Tauri development, run:"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"To build the local App and DMG, install the two Rust targets once, then run the build:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Open `src-tauri/target/universal-apple-darwin/release/bundle/macos/Codex Taskboard.app` from Finder."},{"id":"p38s2","text":" The DMG is in `src-tauri/target/universal-apple-darwin/release/bundle/dmg/`. If you only want the s"},{"id":"p38s3","text":"table App, download the current DMG from GitHub Releases."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"The App contains its own Node runtime, Taskboard service, built web UI, Skill, CLI wrapper, and inje"},{"id":"p39s2","text":"ction script. It starts the service, reuses an open Codex with a reachable CDP renderer, opens Taskb"},{"id":"p39s3","text":"oard in the native browser panel of an ordinary Codex without CDP, or launches the official Codex ap"},{"id":"p39s4","text":"p when no Codex is open. It waits for the renderer, injects the sidebar entry when CDP is available,"},{"id":"p39s5","text":" and opens the panel without showing a terminal window. The App can be copied away from this checkou"},{"id":"p39s6","text":"t; the target Mac only needs the official Codex app and does not need this repository, a system Node"},{"id":"p39s7","text":" installation, or a separate Codex CLI installation. Taskboard data is stored in `~/Library/Applicat"},{"id":"p39s8","text":"ion Support/Codex Taskboard`, and launcher output is written to `~/Library/Logs/Codex Taskboard/code"},{"id":"p39s9","text":"x-taskboard-launcher.log`."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"### Linux App: Ubuntu 24.04 x64 packages"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"The first Linux desktop release supports Ubuntu 24.04 LTS on x64 only. Install the official ChatGPT "},{"id":"p41s2","text":"desktop `.deb` first and confirm that `chatgpt` opens it. Then download either the Codex Taskboard `"},{"id":"p41s3","text":".deb` or `.AppImage` from GitHub Releases. Replace `<file>` below with the downloaded filename."},{"id":"p42s1","text":"Install the `.deb` package:"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"Or run the AppImage:"},{"id":"p45s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p46s1","text":"To build both packages on Ubuntu 24.04 x64, run:"},{"id":"p47s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p48s1","text":"This first release does not support ARM64, Fedora, RPM packages, or other Linux distributions."},{"id":"p49s1","text":"### Windows code signing"},{"id":"p50s1","text":"For official Windows releases after the application is approved: **Free code signing provided by Sig"},{"id":"p50s2","text":"nPath.io, certificate by SignPath Foundation.** Current Windows CI artifacts remain unsigned until t"},{"id":"p50s3","text":"hat approval. See the Code signing policy, Privacy policy, and Windows uninstall instructions."},{"id":"p51s1","text":"The local build uses ad-hoc code signing for direct verification. A public macOS download still need"},{"id":"p51s2","text":"s Developer ID signing and Apple notarization."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

